WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
The question: «Faut-il interdire
le téléphone portable au lycée

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.690
?» Should phones be banned in high school?

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.140
Source 1, an audio clip.

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.290
A principal says: «les
élèves sont plus concentrés».

5
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.880
Source 2, an article, calls
the phone a learning tool.

6
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.220
Source 3, an infographic with
illustrative practice figures:

7
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.400
61 percent say it helps with homework.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.330
You hear the audio twice.

9
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.670
You have 55 minutes.

10
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.990
So how do you turn three sources
into an essay that argues,

11
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.900
instead of just retelling?

12
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.800
In this mission, you'll
map the 55 minutes,

13
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.950
countdown included. Then
you'll fill a note grid,

14
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.450
tagging each source «pour»,
«contre» or «nuancé».

15
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.400
Your mission: work out how to
write an essay that argues.
